ts 100000 ≤ B → integer; `integer/sub rc 1` → integer. No doubling is consulted any more |\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:149:| 2^100000 | 100001 | FOREIGN, retained whole | n/a | `integer/add rc 1` → bits 100001 > B → `::bit-limit` → not an integer |\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:160:1. §3, \"With one bit of headroom, reaching the limit takes at least 2^(max-bits-1) acquisitions\" —\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:161:   arithmetically true of the *module limit* and irrelevant: the doubling's own exclusion sat at\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:162:   T, one acquisition from a legally constructible count. sol's re-check6 says this precisely\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:163:   (\"the comments' huge number of acquisitions concerns reaching the arithmetic limit, while\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:165:2. §3 table, \"any beyond-native big carrier under the limit → LOCAL\" — false at 2da48669; T is\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:166:   under the limit and was refused.\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:168:   `::integer/max-bits`\" — true but not sufficient. Deriving a threshold from the limits still\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:171:4. The source comments carrying claims 1-3 (\"crossing the limit unreachable\", \"No count the\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-max.findings.md:172:   repaired arithmetic itself produces is ever refused\", \"every still-operable count is admitted\")\ncollab/exception-track/1794533165000-engineer-php-r1r2r3-r12.qwen3.8-m