\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis passes both strict comparisons and Throwable classification. Reception'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\naddref changes the count to 9223372036854775807. Now ordinary PHP source, with no\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrequested numeric operation, fails:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunction receive(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$f) {'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    try { return \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$f(); }'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    catch (Throwable \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$e) { return $e; }'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe synthetic callable delivers the thrown condition through its supplied\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n:yang.call/raise exit. The caught local value reaches lower-return'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s ordinary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nphp/addref, which executes another raw + and overflows. The first acquisition is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nsafe; the consumed path is not.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFirsthand result, current worktree source, parsed/lowered receiver and JVM AST\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nwalker, successful bounded subprocess:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n:source-receiver 1                    :php/null\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n:source-receiver 9223372036854775807  :php/null\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n:source-receiver 9223372036854775806  :failure long overflow nil\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\