ary catch/return \\\\\\\"\\\\n   663\\\\t               \\\\\\\"acquisition with identity preserved\\\\\\\")))))\\\\n   664\\\\t\\\\n   665\\\\t\\\\n   666\\\\t(deftest ^:slow php-nil-condition-reception-test\\\\n   667\\\\t  ;; The steward addendum's F1 nil-guard choice, taken DELIBERATELY as\\\\n   668\\\\t  ;; option (a): a non-map or nil condition delivered to reception is NOT\\\\n   669\\\\t  ;; provenance-minted (nil provenance is refused by the reserved door —\\\\n   670\\\\t  ;; an operational failure that would escape the boundary behavior); it\\\\neight exception-track briefs/spec/findings records. Runtime regions are function entry,\\\\nClosure entry, reception through the three helpers, retention helpers, host-door declaration,\\\\nand the seeded exception hierarchy. This is consistent with the supplied PHP round and\\\\nadoption briefs. No shared kit, design doctrine, scanner golden, ledger, or other frontend\\\\nimplementation was edited. `git diff --check 0e666a3f..4939a3ae` passed.\\\\n\\\\nThe referenced region registry\\\\n`collab/exception-track/1794343000000-exception-track-surface-registry.md` is absent from\\\\nthis worktree and from the reviewed base. Its literal region list cannot be certified here;\\\\nscope was checked against the available binding briefs and actual diff instead.\\\\n\\\\nGate tables are plausible as scoped engineer reports, not independently reproduced gate\\\\nresults. The hard-rule parity pin (:298) uses the kit boundary and parsed PHP bare rethrow,\\\\nasserts the fully qualified reason and condition identity, and checks all three backends.\\\\nThe clone/mutation pins inspect guest identity before rendering. Test data and assertions\\\\nwere not weakened by r2/r3. The reported Node/Dart/remote and slow-corpus gaps are explicit.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n59:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_30\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path\\\\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone, timedelta\\\\np=Path(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/private/tmp/phpexc-review/collab/exception-track/1794527358000-architect-step7-recheck5.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\nassert not p.exists(), \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Refusing to overwrite an existing findings artifact\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\nnow=datetime.now(timezone.utc)\\\\nheader=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Created-GMT: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"+now.strftime(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCreated-Local: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"+now.astimezone(timezone(timedelta(hours=7))).strftime(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S +0700 (Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\np.write_text(header+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Coding-Agent: codex (gpt-6.1-sol)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSession-ID: unavailable in this environment\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRole: Architect, read-only step-7 re-check round 5\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nReviewed-Base: 265c4a4590259f2ea592cb81cd6991aa7b8afde8\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nReviewed-Tip: 59329a054a66041cb2c5816aae0e97dc65e2b542\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nVerdict: RESIDUALS — NOT MERGE-READY\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n# Step-7 re-check round 5\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe exact-integer repair closes both concrete count-domain defects from re-check 4:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nordinary acquisition no longer uses native overflowing/mixed-carrier arithmetic, and a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncomputed Ratio is rejected before integer/compare. However, I rule AGAINST the restored\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nendpoint disposition. One P2 residual remains: a value admitted and returned as the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\noriginal local Exception becomes ForeignException on its next ordinary reception because\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe first reception moved its count onto the excluded maximum. This was reproduced\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthrough parsed/lowered PHP source at the reviewed tip.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe source and tests were reviewed read-only. Only this requested findings artifact was\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nwritten; no source, tests, fixtures, configuration, caches, or git history were modified.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## P2 residual — ordinary ownership changes turn a local exception into a foreign one\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nLocation: src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc:2937-2939.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nConsumer: php.rt/receive-condition at :2975-2977.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nCoverage gap: test/yang/call/php_exception_test.clj:627-644 exercises only one reception.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe test'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s own near-max payload is sufficient:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```clojure'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(assoc {} :php/obj\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       (cell/new (assoc {:class \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Exception\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                       :rc (integer/parse \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"9223372036854775806\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSupply its thrown condition through a callable'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s actual :yang.call/raise exit, and call\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthis ordinary PHP receiver TWICE with the same callable/condition:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```php'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfunction receive(\\\\\\\"'$f) {'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    try { return \\\\\\\"'$f(); }'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    catch (Throwable \\\\\\\"'$e) { return $e; }'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nKeep the first returned value live while making the second call. No count edits, numeric\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\noperations, or malformed-condition tricks occur between the two calls. Firsthand results\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nfrom current-tip source, production host registry and JVM AST walker:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Initial count | First result identical | Count after first return | Second result identical | Second class |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| 1 | true | 2 | true | Exception |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| 9223372036854775806 | true | 9223372036854775807 | **false** | **ForeignException** |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| 9007199254740992 | true | 9007199254740993 | true | Exception |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe failing case completed normally at the VM level; this is a semantic identity failure,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnot another host overflow. Its count after the second call remains 9223372036854775807.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nA separate parserless two-reception probe gave the same classification failure.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe first call proves exactly why the engineer'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s claim that the endpoint is \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"not a count\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nphp'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s machinery could have produced\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" is false: php'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s own repaired ownership operations\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\njust produced it. The value is still throwable by php/throw-value, which checks the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThrowable hierarchy and uses the repaired exact addref. Only boundary reception changes\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nits class/identity. An ordinary catch retaining one more reference cannot make an otherwise\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nunchanged local exception foreign.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Endpoint ruling\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nSection 8.10.7 rule 1 and the owner ruling v2 R2 require already-local exceptions to retain\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nordinary catching and identity. Rule 3 applies to an OTHERWISE-foreign payload; it does\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnot authorize reclassifying this runtime-produced state just because its private reference\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncount reached the source-language integer endpoint.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe accepted Python implementation at prelude.cljc:1067-1079 recognizes its own exception\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrepresentation/hierarchy and raises that value unchanged. It has no PHP reference-count\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nanalogue that would justify a signed-64-bit cutoff on PHP'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s now-exact ownership arithmetic.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nPHP still needs representation and operability checks; that does not make every previous\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncount cutoff a semantic invariant after its original arithmetic reason has been removed.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nI therefore rule the other way on the handover question: the signed-64-bit endpoints,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nby themselves, are not a reason to wrap an otherwise admitted Throwable under the repaired\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\narithmetic. The positive maximum counterexample alone is enough to reject the restored\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\npolicy. The minimum-only exclusion likewise lacks the old decrement-overflow justification;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nany separately proposed count invariant must be justified consistently, not inferred from\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe old host carrier limits.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nRequired completion:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Preserve exact integer/add and integer/sub and the exact-integer admission predicate.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Make reception preserve local type/identity across ordinary acquisitions and later\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  receptions, including the runtime-produced endpoint and beyond-native results.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Extend the near-max source pin to two calls while the first result remains live, with\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  original identity and original Exception class on BOTH results.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Keep endpoint coverage, but revise its asserted disposition under this ruling instead\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  of deleting the cases. Keep malformed, competing-marker, ratio, missing/non-number and\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  legitimate-local controls with complete-condition/evidence/payload checks for foreign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  cases.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThis revises the old endpoint disposition explicitly in response to the requested ruling;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nit is not permission to silently invert or remove unrelated pins.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Do not apply the documented bare revert without a limit-aware replacement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe engineer is correct about the separate integer-module limit hazard: integer/integer?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrecognizes carriers without checking ::integer/max-bits; integer/add and integer/sub can\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nreturn ::bit-limit. Installing that keyword as :rc would make the next integer operation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrefuse. Merely deleting both bounds and accepting EVERY exact integer is not a complete fix.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThat hazard does not justify the particular strict 64-bit boundary: MAX, MAX+1 and MIN are\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nwell inside the profile'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s minimum 4096-bit arithmetic limit. Count validation/limit handling\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nmust distinguish genuinely unsupported state from the local results ordinary ownership\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnow produces. No broad host catch is authorized.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nTwo details in the findings'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' supporting argument should also be corrected:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n(1) raw clojure.core/* on two Long operands does not auto-promote past overflow; a BigInt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nseed is needed for the proposed repeated-squaring construction; (2) an initial 63-bit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nbound does not prove ALL subsequent ownership results stay 64-bit. Neither correction\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nnegates the real ::bit-limit hazard, and neither is the blocking reproduction above.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Ruling 1 — both re-check-4 count-domain counterexamples are repaired\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nphp/addref (:1856-1857) and php/delref (:1869) now use the integer module. Its checked big\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\npath promotes operands to the host big carrier, computes exactly, and demotes to the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncanonical carrier; its fast path falls back when the safe native result range is exceeded.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe ordinary lower-return acquisition still calls php/addref (lower.cljc:2945), so the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrepair applies after reception as required, including copying/rethrow operations using it.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe source receiver above now completes its FIRST near-max call with original identity;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe previous native-long overflow is closed. The 2\\\\\\\"'^53 decimal also completes with original'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nidentity through both calls on the JVM.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFor JS, dao.host.integer/exact-integer? admits BigInt, promote keeps both arithmetic\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\noperands in BigInt form, and demote produces the canonical Number/BigInt result. Thus the\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ncount is no longer sent to raw BigInt-plus-Number arithmetic. integer/sub demotes zero to\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe native zero, preserving the existing (= n 0) destruction test. This is verified by\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nreading the actual host/module implementations; no complete Node/Dart runtime green is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclaimed by this review. The decimal in the JVM pin is a Long and alone would not prove JS.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAt :2936 integer/integer? now precedes BOTH integer/compare calls. Its implementation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndelegates directly to host/exact-integer?, so a computed JVM Ratio, float64 content, a\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nDouble, nil, or a non-number never reaches those comparisons. The old representation\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nclassifier php/int? and the broad data/number? check are gone from count admission.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nFirsthand direct reception controls, including full evidence and payload identity:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| Count expression | ForeignException | Original local identity | Whole condition retained | Original payload retained |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| (/ 1 2) | true | false | true | true |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| (data/float64 1) | true | false | true | true |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| (data/float-value 1) | true | false | true | true |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| (/ 6 3) | false | true | n/a | n/a |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| parse MAX | true | false | true | true |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n| parse MIN | true | false | true | true |\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe last two rows record CURRENT behavior, which the endpoint ruling above rejects;\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe retention machinery itself works on those rejected paths. The computed-ratio\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nresidual is CLOSED, not merely hidden behind another refusal.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Ruling 3 — accept leaving finalize\\\\\\\"'!'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''s raw unpin in this round\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAt prelude.cljc:4382 finalize\\\\\\\"'! overwrites :rc with the literal native 1 BEFORE invoking'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe destructor. The raw subtraction at :4386 therefore does not consume the large count\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nadmitted from a boundary. Under ordinary PHP ownership, only acquisitions/releases made\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nduring this destructor contribute to its unpin value.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nI accept that scoped argument for the requested residual: the near-max and JS-BigInt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nreceived-carrier counterexamples cannot flow into this subtraction. No conversion is\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nrequired for this review. This is not a proof against arbitrary guest cell/set\\\\\\\"'! corruption'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nduring a destructor, nor an unrestricted totality claim for an unbounded number of\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nacquisitions. Neither is the counterexample established here.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n## Ruling 4 — pins, publication surface and scope\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nThe requested range is one commit and exactly three changed files: the PHP prelude,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nthe PHP exception test, and the r10 findings. No other frontend, VM implementation,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nlowerer, shared kit, fixture, ledger, or desig