\\\"}}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:29:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1830,1920p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; sed -n '2912,3015p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; cat collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md; rg -n '8.10.7' docs/design/*.md; ls -a .cpcache; ls /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-phpexc/build\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:30:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_14\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"sed -n '1830,1920p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; sed -n '2912,3015p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; cat collab/exception-track/1794960000000-owner-ruling-exception-uniformity-v2.md; rg -n '8.10.7' docs/design/*.md; ls -a .cpcache; ls /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-phpexc/build\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"     ;; a cell `destroy` has entered: its count is frozen (cycle-safe teardown)\\n     (fn [x]\\n       (let [c (php/cell-of x)]\\n         (if (nil? c) false (= (get (cell/get c) :released?) true))))]\\n    [php/addref\\n     ;; the count arithmetic is the engine's EXACT-INTEGER arithmetic, not\\n     ;; the raw host +/-: integer/add promotes both operands to the host\\n     ;; big integer and demotes the result, so it is exact over every\\n     ;; exact-integer carrier on every supported host (JVM longs and big\\n     ;; carriers, JS safe numbers and BigInts, Dart ints and BigInts) —\\n     ;; no native overflow at the long maximum and no BigInt/Number mixing\\n     ;; on JS. That is what makes a count safe for its WHOLE ownership\\n     ;; life instead of for one step: reception's acquisition can put a\\n     ;; count AT the native long maximum, and the next ordinary\\n     ;; acquisition — the lowerer wraps every returned expression in\\n     ;; php/addref, and copies and rethrows acquire too — puts it past,\\n     ;; into the host big carrier, where the raw host + threw. A count\\n     ;; that far is ordinary local state this arithmetic produced, so\\n     ;; admission cuts nothing off at a carrier boundary; php/obj-val?\\n     ;; probes instead that the count is operable under the composition's\\n     ;; own integer limits. The fast kernels keep the common small-count\\n     ;; path native.\\n     (fn [x]\\n       (let [c (php/cell-of x)]\\n         (if (nil? c)\\n           x\\n           (if (php/released? x)\\n             x\\n             (do (cell/set! c (assoc (cell/get c)\\n                                     :rc (integer/add (get (cell/get c) :rc) 1)))\\n                 x)))))]\\n    [php/delref\\n     ;; the same exact domain as addref. A count only ever reaches 0 in\\n     ;; the native carrier (integer/sub demotes a result inside the host's\\n     ;; native range), so the zero test below is carrier-uniform.\\n     (fn [x]\\n       (let [c (php/cell-of x)]\\n         (if (nil? c)\\n           :php/null\\n           (if (php/released? x)\\n             :php/null\\n             (let [n (integer/sub (get (cell/get c) :rc) 1)]\\n               (do (cell/set! c (assoc (cell/get c) :rc n))\\n                   (if (= n 0) (php/destroy x) :php/null)))))))]\\n    [php/release-slots\\n     ;; DELREF the slots of `tbl` named by `deps` (a key map, or :all)\\n     (fn [tbl deps i n]\\n       (if (< i n)\\n         (let [kk (get (get tbl :order) i)]\\n           (do (if (= deps :all)\\n                 (php/delref (get (get tbl :index) kk))\\n                 (if (nil? (get deps kk))\\n                   :php/null\\n                   (php/delref (get (get tbl :index) kk))))\\n               (php/release-slots tbl deps (+ i 1) n)))\\n         :php/null))]\\n    [php/destroy\\n     ;; the cell is marked released BEFORE its slots are, so a cycle back to it\\n     ;; (row 18) finds it released and stops\\n     (fn [x]\\n       (let [k (php/slot-kind x)]\\n         (if (= k :arr-handle)\\n           (let [c (get x :php/arr)\\n                 st (cell/get c)]\\n             (do (cell/set! c (assoc st :released? true))\\n                 (php/release-slots (get st :value) (get st :deps) 0\\n                                    (php/array-count (get st :value)))))\\n           (if (= k :ref-marker)\\n             (let [c (get x :php/ref)]\\n               (do (cell/set! c (assoc (cell/get c) :released? true))\\n                   (php/delref (php/ref-value x))))\\n             (if (= k :obj-handle) (php/destroy-obj x) :php/null)))))]\\n    [php/destroy-obj\\n     ;; DESTROY: run the destructor once (pinned), then free unless resurrected\\n     (fn [x]\\n       (let [st (cell/get (get x :php/obj))]\\n         (if (get st :released?)\\n           :php/null\\n           (if (if (get st :destructed?)\\n                 false\\n                 (not (nil? (php/class-method (php/class-lookup (get st :class)) \\\"__destruct\\\"))))\\n             (php/finalize! x)\\n             (php/free-obj x)))))]\\n    [php/free-obj\\n     (fn [x]\\n       (let [c (get x :php/obj)\\n             st (cell/get c)\\n             props (get st :props)]\\n         (if (get st :released?)\\n           :php/null\\n           (do (cell/set! c (assoc (assoc st :destructed? true) :released? true))\\n     ;; one domain they all operate in, ever reaches the Throwable test,\\n     ;; and no unauthenticated or unvalidated dereference or arithmetic\\n     ;; ever happens.\\n     (fn [v]\\n       (if (if (not (nil? (get v :php/ref))) true (not (nil? (get v :php/arr))))\\n         false\\n         (if (nil? (get v :php/obj))\\n           (if (= (get v :php/type) :obj)\\n             (data/string? (get v :class))\\n             false)\\n           (if (cell/authentic? (get v :php/obj))\\n             (let [st (cell/get (get v :php/obj))]\\n               (if (data/string? (get st :class))\\n                 (let [rc (get st :rc)]\\n                   ;; integer/integer? FIRST: it is the total domain\\n                   ;; predicate of the integer/add calls below, which\\n                   ;; refuse any carrier it rejects. A php representation\\n                   ;; classifier cannot stand in for it: a computed ratio\\n                   ;; passes data/number? AND php/int? (php/kind's float64\\n                   ;; content test), and the integer primitives then refuse\\n                   ;; it — the reception-introduced failure of the\\n                   ;; re-check4 counterexample.\\n                   ;; The two probes that follow are limit-aware, and they\\n                   ;; are what replaces r7's native-carrier bounds without\\n                   ;; reverting to \\\"every exact integer\\\". The first IS\\n                   ;; addref's own operation, so admission establishes r7's\\n                   ;; property — an INCREMENTABLE count — against this\\n                   ;; composition's actual arithmetic domain rather than\\n                   ;; against the host carrier: past ::integer/max-bits\\n                   ;; integer/add answers the ::bit-limit keyword instead of\\n                   ;; an integer, and installing that as :rc would make the\\n                   ;; next ownership operation refuse as a host failure\\n                   ;; escaping the boundary. The second proves a full bit of\\n                   ;; HEADROOM (|rc| < 2^(max-bits - 1)), because an\\n                   ;; admission-time increment is not an invariant: counts\\n                   ;; grow by one per acquisition, so a count admitted at\\n                   ;; the very limit could creep past it later. With one bit\\n                   ;; of headroom, breaching the limit takes at least\\n                   ;; 2^(max-bits - 1) acquisitions, which no run reaches —\\n                   ;; and delref's decrement is covered by the same\\n                   ;; headroom. No count the repaired arithmetic itself\\n                   ;; produces is ever refused: MAX, MIN and the\\n                   ;; beyond-native big carriers all double inside the\\n                   ;; limit, so they stay LOCAL (§8.10.7 rule 1).\\n                   (if (integer/integer? rc)\\n                     (if (integer/integer? (integer/add rc 1))\\n                       (integer/integer? (integer/add rc rc))\\n                       false)\\n                     false))\\n                 false))\\n             false))))]\\n    [php.rt/receive-condition\\n     ;; §8.10.7 reception, shared by every php call helper: classify the\\n     ;; delivered condition and continue it as a local Throwable. A\\n     ;; :yang.call/thrown payload that is itself a PHP Throwable keeps its\\n     ;; ordinary catching and identity behavior — raised unchanged, no\\n     ;; wrapper (crossing back into php restores the original type and\\n     ;; identity). Any other payload — an otherwise-foreign exception or a\\n     ;; plain foreign value, whatever its representation — becomes the\\n     ;; prelude-owned ForeignException retaining the complete original\\n     ;; condition; the protocol reasons map to the documented local Error.\\n     ;; Both generated forms mint through php.rt/mint-retained, so the\\n     ;; condition rides the VM provenance slot of the wrapper's identity\\n     ;; cell and an unchanged rethrow forwards the original condition — the\\n     ;; entry bridge consults the same provenance read — with no wrapper\\n     ;; stacking. A returned condition-shaped map never reaches here: it is\\n     ;; ordinary data.\\n     ;; The name is `php.rt/*`, never a module export (the step-7 P1): a\\n     ;; guest-reachable receiver would be a transitive mint — a forged\\n     ;; condition called through it would ride a GENUINE provenance-carrying\\n     ;; wrapper. Only the three call helpers reference it, as the raise\\n     ;; exit they hand to yang.call/invoke, where every condition it sees\\n     ;; is bridge- or validation-built, never a guest argument.\\n     ;; The steward's nil-guard choice, taken DELIBERATELY as option (a):\\n     ;; the condition is shape-checked BEFORE any mint — a nil or non-map\\n     ;; condition raises the plain local TypeError with NO provenance mint\\n     ;; (nil provenance is refused by the reserved door as an operational\\n     ;; failure, which would escape the boundary behavior); only a\\n     ;; map-shaped condition is ever retained or forwarded.\\n     (fn [condition]\\n       (if (data/map? condition)\\n         (if (= (get condition :yang.call/reason) :yang.call/thrown)\\n           (let [v (get condition :yang.call/value)]\\n             (if (if (php/obj-val? v) (php/throwable? v) false)\\n               (php/raise (php/addref v))\\n               (php.rt/raise-foreign condition)))\\n           (php.rt/raise-protocol condition))\\n         (php/throw-error \\\"TypeError\\\" \\\"Invalid condition delivered to reception\\\")))]\\n    [php/call\\n     (fn [f args]\\n       (yang.call/invoke f args [] php.rt/receive-condition))]\\n    [php/call-with-binding-profile\\n     (fn [f args named binding-profile]\\n       (yang.call/invoke-with f args named php.rt/receive-condition\\n                              (assoc {} :yang.call/binding-profile binding-profile)))]\\n    ;; the internal array pointer (row 55): an ordinal in the table's `:ptr`,\\n    ;; so it travels with the value (copy, DUP, upgrade); absent means 0\\n    [php/ptr-of\\n     (fn [arr] (let [p (get (php/arr-table arr) :ptr)] (if (nil? p) 0 p)))]\\n    [php/ptr-set\\n     (fn [arr p]\\n       (if (= (php/slot-kind arr) :arr-handle)\\n         (let [c (get arr :php/arr)\\n               st (cell/get c)]\\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-07 04:30:00 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-07 11:30:00 +07 (+0700)\\nStatus: OWNER-APPROVED 2026-11-07 (\\\"enforce everywhere consistently. this should be a separate track.\\\"); v2 SUPERSEDES v1 (1794920000000) per the review round — architect gpt-6-astra, engineer mob gpt-6.1-sol + gemini-3.8-flash: all three ACCEPT WITH AMENDMENTS, folded below. Qwen aborted (headless tool denial); kimi quota-exhausted (429).\\nReview records: collab/exception-track/1794930000000-architect-exception-ruling-review.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log, 1794930000000-engineer-exception-ruling-review.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log, 1794930000000-engineer-exception-ruling-review.gemini-3.8-flash.stdout.log.\\n\\n# RULING OF RECORD v2 — the exception track: §8.10.7 enforced uniformly in all four frontends\\n\\n## The decision\\n\\nException handling is enforced uniformly across yang.clojure, yang.typescript (js),\\nyang.php, and yang.python. At every admitted guest-call boundary, an escaping source\\nexception compiles down to THE SAME continuation: the caller's supplied raise exit\\nreceiving the §8.10.7 condition\\n\\n    {:yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown, :yang.call/value original-thrown-value}\\n\\nand every receiving runtime implements the §8.10.7 reception rules as written. This is a\\nSEPARATE TRACK: its own folder (collab/exception-track/), its own rounds, its own\\nacceptance gate; the four frontend seats cede the exception-fix surfaces to the track and\\nreceive per-frontend results back into their records.\\n\\n## Scope bounds (v2: sharpened per astra §5)\\n\\n- \\\"Every boundary\\\" means ADMITTED GUEST-CALL boundaries. VM/custody defects and host\\n  implementation failures remain operational failures (design :3904); no broad\\n  host catch-and-relabel is authorized.\\n- A RETURNED condition-shaped map is ordinary data; a THROWN condition-shaped map is the\\n  payload of a fresh condition; shape is never evidence of an existing condition to\\n  forward (the cell-ref rule, restated — R5).\\n- \\\"Same continuation\\\" does NOT require identical internal lowering (R4's allowance).\\n\\n## The requirements (v2: amended per the review round)\\n\\n**R1 — the callee bridge (js AND php non-compliant today).** Every frontend's published\\nfunction entry, closure entry, and higher-order entry installs the exception bridge\\nBEFORE argument binding: it reads the supplied `:yang.call/raise` and delivers every\\nescaping source exception AND argument-binding failure to it as the thrown condition,\\nexactly once, with execution after the call unreachable. js entries apply `:code` without\\nreading the raise exit (prelude.cljc:1581); php's function entry (:2264) and Closure entry\\n(:4217) lack it, and php's raise with an empty handler stack RETURNS normally\\n(prelude.cljc:194-197). The bridge must also satisfy §8.10.8: complete cleanup and\\nhandler/depth/frame restoration BEFORE the transfer; a later generator resume never\\nreuses a raise exit belonging to a completed call.\\n\\n**R2 — foreign reception and retained-condition lifetime (python, php non-compliant\\ntoday).** On receiving a thrown condition: (1) a payload valid in the receiving runtime\\nkeeps its ordinary catching and identity behavior — delivered UNCHANGED (python raising\\nan already-local exception raw is compliant; python raising an OTHERWISE-FOREIGN payload\\nraw at :1034 is not); (2) js may deliver the otherwise-foreign payload raw; (3) python\\nand php represent an otherwise-foreign payload with their own generated\\n`ForeignException`, retaining the complete condition and original payload — catch-all\\ncatches it, typed catches match the LOCAL hierarchy, never guessed foreign class names,\\nand formatting it never implicitly invokes foreign methods. Retention rides the generated\\nexception's IDENTITY for its ENTIRE LIFETIME, outside source-writable attributes, with no\\nambient registry (design :3878, :3885). Raising the whole envelope (php :2384) or an\\notherwise-foreign raw payload (python :1034) is non-compliant.\\n\\n**R3 — protocol failures retain and forward the condition (ALL FOUR frontends; v2\\nwidened per astra §1 / sol §1).** `:yang.call/not-callable`, `:yang.call/invalid-invocation`,\\n`:yang.call/unsupported-binding` (fully qualified) map to a documented local exception\\nform retaining the complete original condition — qualified reason AND plain evidence — so\\nan unchanged rethrow FORWARDS the original condition without a new wrapper. js discards\\nthe condition into fresh text (:1627); python builds a generic TypeError (:1046); clojure\\nretains it as catch data (:1306) but public escape reclassifies through unconditional\\n`yang.call/thrown` (:1088); php constructs a fresh Error for not-callable and raises the\\nenvelope otherwise (:2384), and its source rethrow rejects that envelope (:4085). All\\nfour are in scope, reception AND outbound rethrow.\\n\\n**R4 — clojure unifies or proves equivalence.** The intra-unit outcome-token channel\\n(clojure.cljc:1115, :1125-1133) may remain an optimization only with equivalence proof\\nacross caught/uncaught throws, protocol rethrow, binding failures, and higher-order\\nre-entry (§8.10.9's bar) — a single passing example is insufficient. Public\\nprotocol-rethrow repair (R3) does not wait for this decision. Clojure's restricted catch\\nsurface (single catch, no `finally`) is a source-semantics decision this ruling does not\\nchange.\\n\\n**R5 — no new shape-routing.** Per the scope bounds above; plus: forged or\\nsource-writable attributes on a wrapper-looking value never authenticate a retained\\ncondition.\\n\\n## The baseline (audit of record)\\n\\nThe gpt-6.1-sol audit (collab/yang-python/1794900000000, verdict DIVERGENT, HEAD\\ne9a0b430) is the baseline. Citation corrections of record from the review round: js\\nfollows its GUEST continuation handler stack (js.rt/ctx, prelude.cljc:1704), not the host\\nengine's; php's empty-stack return is :194-197 (envelope reception :2384); clojure's\\nactual private branches are :1115 and :1125-1133 (:1110 is the packet-length guard).\\n\\n## Acceptance gate (v2: widened per astra §4 / sol §4)\\n\\nThe track is DONE when ALL of the following hold, with real source on both sides of every\\nleg:\\n\\n1. **The directed pair matrix — 12 cross-language directions** derived from the four\\n   admitted frontends (clojure↔python and clojure↔php explicitly included), plus local\\n   regressions.\\n2. **Callable-kind coverage**: named exports AND closure/higher-order entries (php\\n   Closures concretely), supported methods/callable objects per frontend capability.\\n3. **The §8.10.11 exception scenarios**: binding failures; arbitrary foreign thrown\\n   data; catch-all and typed catches (where the source has them — js has no typed-catch\\n   syntax, clojure's admitted surface rejects `finally`; exercise cleanup in a frontend\\n   that supports it and PRESERVE clojure's rejection tests); unchanged rethrow; finally\\n   replacement; protocol-error rethrow; condition-shaped thrown maps staying data;\\n   A→B→A propagation asserting original identity and cleanup order; the stored\\n   ForeignException rethrown from another activation.\\n4. **Context lifetime**: repeated success→raise→success, cross-runtime recursion,\\n   suspension/resume — handler/depth/frame state restored, exactly-once\\n   binding/cleanup.\\n5. **Host-by-VM results**: JVM, Node, and Dart across the admitted VM paths, with\\n   explicit refusals; portable parser-produced fixtures where the JVM-only kit cannot\\n   reach; bundled-walker paths where admitted, never requiring unsupported linked\\n   execution; bundled/linked parity and task isolation preserving existing custody\\n   refusals.\\n6. **Identity assertions BEFORE rendering**: original reasons, complete evidence, payload\\n   identity, wrapper non-stacking, cleanup order — equal rendered text is not identity\\n   evidence.\\n\\n## Sequencing (v2: corrected per astra §3 / sol §3 — the v1 order is REJECTED)\\n\\n0. Contract + focused FAILING fixtures first (retained-condition provenance; boundary\\n   fixtures construct malformed invocations source cannot naturally build).\\n1. **JS R1 + R3** together (R3 alone cannot cross the boundary while entries ignore the\\n   exit).\\n2. **PHP R1 + R2 + R3 as ONE coherent round** — function entry, Closure entry, and all\\n   three call helpers (php/call, call-with-binding-profile, call-named). Landing the\\n   bridge before reception repair would route local Throwables into the envelope-raising\\n   receiver and break existing local typed catches.\\n3. **Python R2 + R3 with the egress change** (prelude.cljc:912's always-fresh condition\\n   must become condition-preserving for retained wrappers).\\n4. **Clojure R3, then R4** (the optimization decision last).\\nJS and Python work proceed independently once the contract lands; no Clojure-containing\\npair declares conformance before its R3 gap closes.\\n\\n— filed by the yang.python orchestrator seat; owner decision 2026-11-07\\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3678:  guest exit, accepting the condition in section 8.10.7. It closes over\\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3838:#### 8.10.7 Normal return and escaping conditions\\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:3923:inner exception as specified in section 8.10.7.\\nls: .cpcache: No such file or directory\\nantlr\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/exception-track/1794532719000-architect-step7-recheck6.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:32:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_15\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 -c 'import json,pathlib\\nfor line in pathlib.Path(\\\\\\\"collab/exception-track/1794527358000-architect-step7-recheck5.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\\\\\\").read_text().splitlines():\\n try: d=json.loads(line)\\n except: continue\\n i=d.get(\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\",{})\\n if d.get(\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\")==\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\" and i.get(\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\")==\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"clojure.main\\\\\\\" in i.get(\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\",\\